         <draw w="203.2mm" h="41.169mm">
            <value>
               <text>This serves as formal authorization for the department/operating area identified below to act as a “University Cash Collection Point” and accept cash and cash equivalents. All cash and cash equivalents must be collected, processed, documented, secured, and deposited in a timely manner in accordance with the requirements of Integrated California State University Administrative Manual (ICSUAM) Sections 3101.02 and 3102.01 through 3102.06 as well as the University’s Cash Management Policy. All cash and cash equivalents must be deposited with the Main Cashier’s Office (UH-180) using the assigned CASHNet Item Code(s) and campus Deposit Form or with the campus approved armored carrier service. In addition, all designated University Cash Collection Points are subject to periodic review by the Controller’s Office. Designation as a University Cash Collection Point may be discontinued at any time should the department/operating area fail to comply with CSU and University policies. For additional cash handling training, please contact the Controller’s Office or the Director of Student Financial Services.</text>
            </value>
